course: dictionary
lesson: 4804
title: Hummingbird: a word in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hummingbird is a very small, brightly coloured bird from the Americas. Its name gives you a clue: it beats its wings so fast that they hum.
explain: Read this sentence: «Hummingbirds drink nectar from long tube-shaped flowers.» Nectar is a sweet liquid inside flowers, and the long, thin beak of the hummingbird fits into the long flower tubes to reach it.
explain: «Hummingbirds beat their wings up to about 80 times a second, and they can fly backwards.» The clue is in the action: a bird that can stay in one place in the air is hovering. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A hummingbird is a very small, brightly coloured bird from the Americas.
fact: «Hover» means to stay in one place in the air.
fact: Hummingbirds beat their wings very fast, so fast that they make a humming sound.
fact: Hummingbirds drink nectar from flowers and get pollen on their heads as they feed.
fact: The bee hummingbird from Cuba is the smallest bird in the world, and it lives only in the Americas.
exercise: What is a hummingbird? | A kind of flower that hums | *A very small, brightly coloured bird from the Americas | A sea animal with a long tail | A large bird that cannot fly
exercise: Why do hummingbirds hum? | They hum to call their mothers | *Their wings beat so fast that they make a humming sound | Their beaks make a loud whistle | A hummingbird hums when it is happy
exercise: «Hummingbirds drink nectar from long tube-shaped flowers.» Find and copy the word that means the sweet liquid they drink from flowers. | tube | wings | *nectar | pollen
test: «The bee hummingbird from Cuba is the smallest bird in the world.» What is the smallest bird in the world? | A sparrow | *A bee hummingbird | A duck | An ostrich
test: Hummingbirds save energy at night in a deep sleep called torpor. What is torpor? | A loud song | A fast flight over the sea | A kind of flower | *A deep sleep that saves energy at night
exam: «A hummingbird egg is about the size of a jellybean.» What is a hummingbird egg about the size of? | An ostrich egg | A grain of rice | A football | *A jellybean
